     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="FR">1. Strengthened efficiency, transparency and effectiveness of the electoral management and administration through improved institutional capacity, digitization, and legislative reforms
1.4 1 (for ISIE&#x2019;s portal and the first module of the financial supervision platform)
ISIE&#x2019;s portal is technically finalized but testing and bug-fixing continues to ensure the portal modules 

2. Enhanced inclusiveness of the electoral process through the participation of vulnerable and marginalized group
2.4The series of events on issuing ID cards for women in rural areas aim to encourage and support authorities in adopting a tested.practical approach to address the challenge of this category of disenfranchised women voters.

2.5 TEAP II completed two knowledge products that provide a new line of thinking on policy towards the inclusion of youth in political and electoral processes: 
- A study on the impact of the digitalization of political communication on the participation of youth in Tunisia. 
- The Project completed the design of the Toolkit for youth on social media during electoral periods and is now in the process of the digitalization of the Toolkit.

3. TEAP II continues to focus on long-term Information and Communications Technology (ICT) platforms to help electoral authorities undertake their responsibilities in a more structured, reliable, transparent, and sustainable way. 
3.1 The factchecking unit was established at HAICA and factchecked 567 media articles.
3.2 TEAP II supported HAICA in putting in place a factchecking unit made up of a team of journalists and IT professionals with regular and ongoing efforts to check news for disinformation and hate speech, and publish the results on a public platform
3.3 The articles factchecked by the HAICA factchecking unit were published on the factchecking webpage Tunisia Check News and its Facebook page. The webpage was viewed 6,078 times. 
3.4 The factchecking unit is currently installing the software necessary for gender-sensitive analysis. 
3.5 The Project supported HAICA in conducting training for 9 journalists on the media monitoring and factchecking methodology.</narrative>
